Title: The Analysis of Metro Manila Vehicular Crash Patterns: Area and Demographic Evaluation of MMDA Incident Data

Intended Audience: Metropolitan Manila Development Authority (MMDA)

Specific Problem: Total Traffic Disruptions and Collision Hazards Across Metro Manila LGUs 

Analytical Questions:
How do temporal peak windows (rush hour vs. off-peak) and collision densities across Metro Manila cities shift between standard workdays (Monday–Friday) and weekends?

To what degree do differences in urban density explain variations in localized collision rates across Metro Manila LGUs, and which cities deviate most from this trend as high-risk anomalies?"

What proportion of total recorded roadway disruptions in Metro Manila is attributable to vehicular stalls and mechanical failures compared to active collisions, and which specific vehicle categories are most susceptible to operational breakdowns?

